{#- The box: one field for anything a reader wants to say to targum, and the four ways
    out of it. It is one file because it stands on two pages — Learn, where it is the
    front door (2026-09-06, design.md §12), and the conversation page, where it is the
    composer — and two copies of a box drift the way two copies of a nav bar did.

    Left to right: the `+`, which brings a file or a recording and prices it here (it
    used to be Upload, a corner of the nav; it is a thing you do while asking, not a
    place, and since 2026-09-06 the Add page is its "More options"); the field; Speak, shown only where the browser records and the reader
    has modern Hebrew to speak (the page's script decides both); and Send, the working
    action, in the accent.

    Set `placeholder` before including. Every id here is what `chat.js` and `box.js`
    look for. -#}
<form class="composer" id="composer">
  <textarea id="say" rows="2" placeholder="{{ placeholder }}" spellcheck="true"
            aria-label="Your message"></textarea>
  {#- A file, a recording or a book, chosen here and priced in place: the Add page's
      job in one press, since 2026-09-06. A link goes in the field like anything else
      said to targum. The card it draws carries "More options", which is the Add page,
      for a translation or a transcript of your own. -#}
  <button type="button" class="chat-bring" id="chat-bring"
          aria-label="Bring a file or a recording" title="Bring a file or a recording">+</button>
  <input type="file" id="chat-file" hidden
         accept=".txt,.md,.markdown,.epub,.mp3,.m4a,.m4b,.aac,.ogg,.opus,.flac,.wav,.mp4,.m4v,.mov,.webm,.mkv">
  {#- Push-to-talk, and called that: a clip goes up, is written down, and comes back
      as a line — seconds, not a conversation. -#}
  <button type="button" class="chat-mic" id="chat-mic" aria-pressed="false" hidden>Speak</button>
  <button type="submit" class="chat-send" id="chat-send">Send</button>
</form>
{#- What went wrong with a line, said under the box in words (§6), never in colour
    alone. -#}
<p class="chat-said" id="chat-said" role="status" hidden></p>
{#- Where the card for a text brought by the + stands on a page with no thread. -#}
<div class="chat-brought" id="chat-brought"></div>
